  "evidence": "TEXT_C: withdraw from the EU to restore full national sovereignty; oppose an EU government/army/constitution and keep the pound permanently; repeal and re‑enact the Human Rights Act to align with British common law and oppose the EU Charter; deterrent sentencing with “life means life” and more visible policing; immigration set solely by the UK with skills‑based admissions and firm, secure‑reception asylum; UK Bill of Rights preventing any transfer of sovereignty; prioritise NATO/US and exit the EU Rapid Reaction Force. TEXT_F: strengthen families and national identity; “in Europe, not run by Europe,” keep the pound and reject the euro; more police, tougher drug laws, honest sentencing with lifelong supervision for serious offenders; asylum via secure reception centres with presumptive refusal from safe countries and a dedicated Removals Agency; defence backing NATO, opposing an EU army outside NATO, exempting forces from the ECHR; constitutional conservatism (English Votes for English Laws, scrap regional assemblies, keep FPTP) with devolution and school/parental choice.",
